          "guid": "mszrv1zeuj9r72r6",
          "message": {
            "text": "changed() guards undefined transitions by reference and only calls the user's equals with two DEFINED values — so equals: (a, b) => a.n === b.n never has to handle undefined.\n\nvalue.revision is the skip-redundant-paint hook, so its bump decision runs the caller-supplied equals. But data is T | undefined (idle, cleared cache key, reset), and equals is typed (a: T, b: T) => boolean — calling it with undefined would both violate the type and force every caller to null-check. The lastData === undefined || next === undefined ? lastData !== next : !eq(...) split resolves undefined→defined, defined→undefined, and undefined→undefined by identity (so idle→idle and same-cache-miss don't bump), and reserves eq for the defined→defined case the caller actually reasons about. The tests \"revision bumps only when data changes (Object.is by default)\" and \"a custom equals dedups structurally-equal payloads\" cover the defined path; \"reset() clears the cache\" exercises the defined→undefined transition.\n",
            "markdown": "`changed()` guards undefined transitions by reference and only calls the user's `equals` with two DEFINED values — so `equals: (a, b) => a.n === b.n` never has to handle `undefined`.\n\n`value.revision` is the skip-redundant-paint hook, so its bump decision runs the caller-supplied `equals`. But `data` is `T | undefined` (idle, cleared cache key, reset), and `equals` is typed `(a: T, b: T) => boolean` — calling it with `undefined` would both violate the type and force every caller to null-check. The `lastData === undefined || next === undefined ? lastData !== next : !eq(...)` split resolves undefined→defined, defined→undefined, and undefined→undefined by identity (so idle→idle and same-cache-miss don't bump), and reserves `eq` for the defined→defined case the caller actually reasons about. The tests \"revision bumps only when data changes (Object.is by default)\" and \"a custom equals dedups structurally-equal payloads\" cover the defined path; \"reset() clears the cache\" exercises the defined→undefined transition.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/async.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 135,
                  "endLine": 137,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  const changed = (next: T | undefined): boolean =>\n    // undefined transitions are handled by reference; two defined values by `eq`.\n    lastData === undefined || next === undefined ? lastData !== next : !eq(lastData, next);"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
